				"content": "### Interpretation\n\n- API panels measure one adapter invocation. SDK-internal retries or physical HTTP attempts are not separate spans or denominator entries.\n- The failure ratio is `failed / (completed + failed)`. Cancelled invocations stay visible in the outcome panel but do not count as failures.\n- Duration includes time while the stream consumer is waiting and any retries performed inside the provider adapter.\n- A blank runtime gauge means no sample was exported for the selected host/time range; it is not converted to zero.\n- The default `canary_id!~\".+\"` selector excludes explicit live-validation series.\n\n### Buffered store commits\n\n- A commit reports one of three shapes. `buffered_append` and `append` add only the new tail; `rewrite` rewrites the whole collection.\n- `rewrite` cost grows with the collection, so a sustained shift toward it is the signal to look for, not the absolute duration alone. A long conversation rewriting on every flush was what made one task rewrite tens of megabytes to add one entry.\n- The commit duration threshold is deliberately below the default one second flush interval: a commit that outlasts the timer that scheduled it means flushes have begun to overlap.\n- Alert rules for these series are provisioned separately; see `dline-alert-rules.yaml`.",
				"mode": "markdown"
			},
			"pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
			"title": "Metric Boundaries",
			"type": "text"
		}
	],
